    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Time fetched:</b> Oct 6, 2026 5:37PM EDT</p><h2>LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/chlorophyll/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Chlorophyll-a concentration (mg/m^3), FIXED absolute scale <b>LOWEST 0.001</b> (dark blue) → 0.01 → 0.1 → <b>1.0</b> → <b>10 bloom</b> (red) → <b>HIGHEST+ 100</b> (deep purple). Each half-decade owns an equal share of the color; displayed values are true concentrations, never altered. High values indicate biomass/activity, not toxins.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA CoastWatch S-NPP+NOAA-20 VIIRS chlorophyll-a NRT gapfilled Daily (ERDDAP nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily), fallback SQ Daily (nesdisVHNSQchlaDaily)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
